WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.980
Only differences in
potential are physical.

2
00:00:03.030 --> 00:00:05.700
Where we put the zero is our choice.

3
00:00:05.750 --> 00:00:08.790
For a point charge, we put
it infinitely far away,

4
00:00:08.840 --> 00:00:09.990
and it works.

5
00:00:10.040 --> 00:00:14.830
Now stretch the charge out into a long,
straight wire that runs on forever.

6
00:00:14.880 --> 00:00:17.920
Try the same choice of zero, and it fails.

7
00:00:17.970 --> 00:00:21.730
Why can't the potential be
zero infinitely far away?

8
00:00:21.780 --> 00:00:25.000
In this mission, you'll turn
a field into a potential,

9
00:00:25.050 --> 00:00:27.130
by integrating along a path.

10
00:00:27.180 --> 00:00:31.060
Then you'll run it backwards, and
get the field from the potential.

11
00:00:31.110 --> 00:00:36.520
Your mission: explain why a wire's
potential can't be zero infinitely far away.
